meta {
  name: 01 - Approved (Clean Case)
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/loan/underwrite
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "description": "Hi, I make about $8000 a month, been at my job 6 years. I pay around $500 a month on existing debts. I want to borrow $10,000 for a kitchen renovation. My credit score is around 750."
  }
}

docs {
  End-to-end happy path: extraction -> rules PASS -> risk score (should be
  LOW/MEDIUM) -> APPROVED -> grounded explanation.

  Check three things in the response:
  1. extractedApplication correctly pulls out 8000, 6, 500, 10000, 750,
     and something like "kitchen renovation"
  2. decision.decision is "APPROVED" with a real (non-null) defaultProbability
  3. explanation reads naturally and only references the actual numbers/decision
}
